---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { nap } from '../content/nap.ts';

const lastUpdated = 'May 5, 2026';
const canonical = 'https://www.graciebarrawhittier.com/privacy/';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Gracie Barra Whittier"
  description="How Gracie Barra Whittier collects, uses, and protects personal information from website visitors and trial students in Whittier, CA."
  canonical={canonical}
  hideStickyCTA={true}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 font-[Inter,system-ui,sans-serif]">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gb-navy">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gb-text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-gb-text leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <p>
          {nap.name} ("we", "us", "our") respects your privacy. This policy
          explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices
          you have. It applies to our website and to people who sign up for our
          programs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          1. Information We Collect
        </h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
          <li>
            <strong>Contact information you give us</strong> through forms on
            this site &mdash; your name, email address, and phone number.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Communications</strong> &mdash; messages you send through
            our forms and conversations with our AI chat assistant, which is
            powered by GoHighLevel.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics data</strong> &mdash; standard web traffic
            information such as page views, clicks, device type, and approximate
            location, collected through Google Analytics 4.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          2. How We Use It
        </h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
          <li>To respond to your questions and confirm your free trial.</li>
          <li>To schedule and remind you about your classes.</li>
          <li>
            To send occasional marketing emails about programs, events, and
            offers. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in any
            email.
          </li>
          <li>
            To improve the website and understand how visitors use it.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          3. Third-Party Services
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We use a small set of trusted services to run this site and contact
          you. Each has its own privacy policy.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
          <li>
            <strong>GoHighLevel</strong> &mdash; powers our contact forms, CRM,
            scheduling, AI chat, and email/SMS messaging.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Analytics</strong> &mdash; helps us measure traffic
            and improve the site.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Maps</strong> &mdash; displays our studio location.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          4. SMS Consent
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you opt in via our forms, you may receive text messages from us
          about your trial, scheduling, and class reminders. Message and data
          rates may apply. You can reply <strong>STOP</strong> at any time to
          opt out, or <strong>HELP</strong> for help. Opting out of SMS does not
          remove you from email or in-person communication.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          5. California Privacy Rights (CCPA)
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          California residents have the following rights regarding their
          personal information:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
          <li>
            <strong>Right to know</strong> what personal information we have
            collected about you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to delete</strong> personal information we hold about
            you, subject to limited exceptions.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to opt out of "sale"</strong> of your personal
            information. We do not sell your personal information.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          To exercise any of these rights, email us at
          <a
            href={`mailto:${nap.email}`}
            class="text-gb-red hover:underline"
          >
            {nap.email}
          </a>
          and we will respond within the timeframe required by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          6. Cookies
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This site uses a small number of cookies, mostly for Google Analytics
          and basic site functionality. You can disable cookies in your browser
          settings at any time. Disabling cookies may affect some site features
          but will not block the rest of the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          7. Data Retention
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We keep contact and trial information for as long as you are an
          active student or prospective student, plus a reasonable period for
          legal, accounting, and follow-up purposes. You can ask us to delete
          your information at any time using the email above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          8. Children's Privacy
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We offer programs for kids ages 3 and up. For students under 13, a
          parent or legal guardian provides their child's information on the
          child's behalf when signing up. We do not knowingly collect personal
          information directly from children under 13 through this website. If
          you believe a child has submitted information without a parent's
          consent, please contact us and we will remove it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-gb-navy">
          9. Contact
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Questions about this Privacy Policy or your information? Reach out:
        </p>
        <address class="mt-3 not-italic">
          <div>{nap.name}</div>
          <div>{nap.address}</div>
          <div>
            Email:
            <a
              href={`mailto:${nap.email}`}
              class="text-gb-red hover:underline"
            >
              {nap.email}
            </a>
          </div>
        </address>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
